::ingredients

(flour; all purpose) 2 cups
(baking powder) 1 1/2tsp
(baking soda) 1/2tsp
# Spices
(cinnamon) 1tsp
(nutmeg) 1/4tsp
(ginger) 1/4tsp
(salt) 1/4tsp
(banana, mashed) 1 1/2 cups / ~4-5 bananas
(egg) 2
(sugar, brown or white) 1 cup
(butter) 1/2 cup
(walnuts, crushed) 1/4 cup
(greasing fat) = (butter) as needed -OR- (oil) as needed

::equipment

(oven)
(bowl) 2
(loaf tin)
(skewer) -OR- (chopstick)

::instructions

(oven) <preheat, 350f / 175c>
{wet} = (egg) + (banana) + (butter) + (sugar)
{wet} <mix, bowl>
{dry} = (flour) + (baking soda) + (baking powder) + (cinnamon) + (nutmeg) + (ginger) + (salt)
{dry} <mix, another bowl>
{batter} = {dry} + {wet}
{batter} <mix, adding wet slowly, until no dry flour remains>
(loaf tin) + (greasing fat) <grease, lightly>
{batter} <pour, loaf tin>
    <bake, ~1h, until wooden skewer or chopstick comes out clean>

::story

Not too sweet. Great for when you have friends over for tea.

